  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>TLV-TVM (Transports Littoral Varois) runs the shortest and most frequent service to Porquerolles, departing from La Tour Fondue on the Giens peninsula — a crossing of about 15 minutes. The company also serves Port-Cros and Le Levant, but from the port of Hyères (Port Gavine landing stage).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to TLV-TVM's FAQ (read 06/11/2026), animals travel free, dogs on a leash and other pets in a carrier; category 1 and 2 dogs must be muzzled and held on a leash by an adult. The timetable pages specify "dogs free but not allowed on the beaches". Once there, restrictions are set by the Port-Cros and Porquerolles National Park. On <strong>Porquerolles</strong>, the Park says dogs must be on a leash on paths and trails and are banned from the beaches. On <strong>Port-Cros</strong>, the Park says dogs are banned outside the village, where leashed access is allowed between the Fort du Moulin and the statue of Saint Joseph.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Port-Cros is very restrictive for dogs (village only); check the National Park's regulations before choosing your island.</div>

      <h2>Tickets, crossings and season</h2>
      <p>The Tour Fondue - Porquerolles return ticket is shown at €24 full fare and €21 reduced on TLV-TVM's ticket office; the return is open (even another day). The crossing takes 15 minutes; to Port-Cros, from Hyères port, 45 minutes (€29 / €25 return). Strollers are free on board; a bike costs extra (€17 for your own). In July-August, bus 67 from Hyères to La Tour Fondue is free with the e-ticket. TLV-TVM relays massif closures on its website on severe fire-risk days (message of 19 August 2026: on Porquerolles, only the lagoons, three large northern beaches and about fifteen kilometres of paths remained open).</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the National Park (official website) limits dogs to the village on Port-Cros, whereas Vedettes Îles d'Or also adds the trail to the dam; TLV-TVM fares vary by season (the €24 fare is the one seen in summer 2026); timetables change by period.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Giens peninsula, with its salt-pan trail, is well suited to a walk before or after the crossing.</p>
